# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Admin SDK credentials. Provide exactly one of the two below.
#
# This server uses the ADMIN SDK, which authenticates as a trusted server
# and BYPASSES Firestore security rules entirely. Whichever credential you
# use here is effectively a master key to every task, registration, tutor
# profile, and invoice in the database. Keep it out of git (this file is
# .env.example, not the real .env — never commit the real one) and scope
# the service account to only what this server needs if your org supports
# custom IAM roles.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Option A: paste the service-account key JSON directly (raw, or base64
# to avoid newline issues in some env var stores). Get it from:
# Firebase Console -> Project settings -> Service accounts -> Generate new private key
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# Option B: point at a key file on disk instead (leave the above blank).
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Auth UID recorded as the actor for admin writes (task creator,
# who marked an invoice paid, etc). Any string that identifies "the admin
# operating this MCP server" is fine — it doesn't need to be a real login,
# since the Admin SDK doesn't check it against Firebase Auth.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_UID=
